5b. ROUND 2 (V6-m4): THE DOWNSTREAM RATINGS READ AT THE INSIDE AIR, record l8r2's least-rating method (each sheet's range INCLUDES its
   own rise and prints no rise at current and no derating curve: the part may add (top - air) K, and the rise at the printed rating is
   taken as the whole span from 25 C to the range's top, the most severe reading the sheet allows; heating as the current squared:
   I_air = I_printed x sqrt((top - air) / (top - 25)), MODEL on PRINTED figures; the rating's own ambient is not printed, 25 C is
   record l8r2's reading, ASSUMPTION). Air: L4-E12 E5's mixed 76.25 C (the case's air; 81.89 C in the exhaust)
   B U23 J_LIME, Wurth 692122030100 VBUS contact: 1.800 A PRINTED, range to 85 C (C_USB3A, C_USB3A_T): 0.6874 A at 76.25 C (0.4098 A at 81.89 C)
        against the load's own demand 0.9534 A: NOT COVERED; against U23's band top 1.3631 A (the most the eFuse passes): NOT COVERED
        the largest air at which the rating covers the demand: 68.2 C; the band's top: 50.6 C (MODEL)
   B U24 J_RB9704's IDC socket contact, Wurth 61201623021: 1.000 A PRINTED, range to 105 C (C_IDC16, C_IDC16_T): 0.5995 A at 76.25 C (0.5375 A at 81.89 C)
        against the load's own demand 0.5000 A: covered; against U24's band top 0.8496 A (the most the eFuse passes): NOT COVERED
        the largest air at which the rating covers the demand: 85.0 C; the band's top: 47.3 C (MODEL)
   B U24 the 16-way flat cable conductor, Wurth 63911615521CAB: 1.000 A PRINTED, range to 105 C (C_RIB16, C_RIB16_T, C_RIB16_D): 0.5995 A at 76.25 C (0.5375 A at 81.89 C)
        against the load's own demand 0.5000 A: covered; against U24's band top 0.8496 A (the most the eFuse passes): NOT COVERED
        the largest air at which the rating covers the demand: 85.0 C; the band's top: 47.3 C (MODEL)
   VENDOR CONDITION (both rows): the makers print no rise at current and no derating curve (the cable sheet only 'current rating
   may decrease due to the derating effect at higher temperatures'); the full-span reading above is the most severe the sheets allow.
   PROVISIONAL (amendment 1): EF-F01's and EF-F02's (c) hold on the printed ratings at 25 C (section 6) and are PROVISIONAL at the inside
   air until the supplier's measurement or a design alternative settles them: the receptacle or harness at the band's top current in a
   76 C chamber, the contact temperature at or under the range's top (85 C, 105 C); alternatives: a USB receptacle whose printed
   rating holds at the inside air (a range to 105 C or a printed derating curve), or J_LIME placed where the local air is bounded
   under the largest air above. No eFuse setting answers U23's row: the LimeSDR's own demand is above the rating's full-span reading.
   For U24 the module's printed 0.500 A is covered; only the eFuse's band top is not, and no TPS2596 setting can put its top under the
   conductor's reading while its foot stays at 0.500 A (the band's ratio of top to foot is 1.272 at R43)
   V6-m5, THE ROCKBLOCK'S CHARGE PADS: the supercapacitors' default charge current about 0.460 A (L_RB_CHG), about 0.800 A with two pads
   bridged (L_RB_CHG_UP); U24's foot 0.6681 A holds the default and NOT the bridged figure: a build condition, the pads OPEN (drafted for
   ASSEMBLY.md in apply_assembly_rb_pads.py, section 8)

